This license covers the original work in this repository: the code in `src/`,
`scripts/`, `tests/`, the root build scripts and launchers, the documentation in
`docs/` and `research/`, and the README. It does NOT cover, and does not grant any
rights to, third-party material referenced or locally cached by this project but
excluded from version control — including HP's BIOS update package, the Supermicro
donor BIOS, Infineon's TPM firmware/tools, and UEFIExtract. Each remains the
property of its respective owner under its own license; see
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and docs/SETUP.md for exactly what that covers and where to
obtain it yourself.

The small extracted donor modules kept under `inputs/core/` (`TrEEPei.pe32`,
`TrEEDxe.pe32` and their `.depex` files) are an exception worth flagging
explicitly: they are binary fragments carved from a third-party vendor BIOS,
kept here only because this project's PEI/DXE drivers depend on them at build
time and because the full donor BIOS they came from is not. They are not
"original work" and are not covered by the MIT grant above either — treat them
under the vendor's own terms. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists the other
vendor-derived files kept under `research/` for analysis.
